-- This is a simple File which contains a program for house price prediction

-- Here I have used Linear Regression and XGBRegressor model to predict the price and find out that XGBRegressor performs best 

-- At first accuracy of the program for both model were low then we have added two Features Manually
         1. Price per Unit Area
         2. Total No of romms
      This both has helped to increase accuracy by approx 25 to 30 percent

-- I have also used here Hyperparameter Tuning for XGBRegressor using GridSearchCV which takes 
         1. grid : parameters
         2. pipeline or model 
         3. cv : No of folds
         4. scoring neg_mean_squared_error 
      This Gives best parameter from the set of parameter that we have given in grid_params

-- I have Separated the Columns containing Categorical and Numerical Values using select_dtypes()

-- I have created two separate pipeline for categorical and Numerical Values which includes imputer and Normailzation
         1. Numerical - StandardScaler, strategy=mean for imputer
         2. Categorical - OneHotEncoding, strategy=most_frequent

-- I have used Column Transformer from compose Library to make run Numerical_pipeline for data with Numericals columns and Categorical_pipeline for data with 
   Categorical Columns

-- SimpleImputer fills missing  values with another value based on strategy 

-- To separate x and y I have drop prices column from table and stored in x (axis = 1)


